40 columns                              |
### comment-attachment scenarios.
>>> Own-line comment leads the next statement.
foo();
// about bar
bar();
<<<
foo();
// about bar
bar();
>>> End-of-line comment trails the preceding argument.
foo(a, // about a
    b);
<<<
foo(
  a, // about a
  b,
);
>>> Remaining comment leads the following argument.
foo(/* x */ a);
<<<
foo(/* x */ a);
>>> Comment in an empty argument list.
foo(/* none */);
<<<
foo(/* none */);
>>> Line comment before a closing bracket.
foo(a, b // last
);
<<<
foo(
  a,
  b, // last
);
>>> Own-line comment between arguments forces a break.
foo(a,
    // about b
    b);
<<<
foo(
  a,
  // about b
  b,
);
>>> Inline block comment keeps a space on each side.
x = a /* note */+ b;
<<<
x = a /* note */ + b;
>>> Blank line before a comment is kept, none after.
foo();

// about bar

bar();
<<<
foo();

// about bar
bar();
